{
  "schema_version": "0.1.0",
  "fixture_id": "ground-access-swing",
  "title": "Bushwick to London: the $157 cheaper ticket leaves from the wrong airport at the wrong hour",
  "pins_down": "Ground access is resolved from the ORIGIN GEOCODE and the LOCAL departure hour against a LIST of modes, and an infeasible mode names the leg that breaks the chain rather than claiming 'no transit'.",
  "as_of": "2026-03-01",
  "notes": [
    "Deliberately dated 2026-03-12: the US moved to DST on Mar 8 and the EU does not until Mar 29, so the NYC-London gap is FOUR hours here, not five. A scorer that assumes a constant offset gets every elapsed time in this file wrong by 60 minutes.",
    "The brief said 'Bushwick to EWR at 6am is a ~$90 car because transit doesn't run.' The reason is wrong and the wrong reason is more dangerous than a wrong number: the NYC subway runs 24 hours and the L runs all night at ~12-minute headways. What actually breaks is the NEW JERSEY end - NJ Transit's Newark Liberty Airport rail stop is served roughly 05:00-01:00, and a 06:10 departure needs you at the terminal around 04:30. The chain fails at its weakest link, and the ledger has to say which link.",
    "The brief also said 'Bushwick to JFK is $2.90.' Two corrections. The MTA base fare became $3.00 on 2026-01-04. And $3.00 only buys the Lefferts Blvd route - three transfers, one of them a bus, roughly 90 minutes - because the JFK AirTrain is free everywhere EXCEPT Jamaica and Howard Beach. The realistic one-transfer path is $11.75. Both are carried, because which one wins is exactly the judgment the scorer exists to make.",
    "Outbound tolls to New Jersey are ZERO. Every Port Authority Hudson and Staten Island crossing is tolled NY-bound only. A symmetric toll model overcharges this trip by about $15 and would wrongly demote every EWR itinerary in the corpus.",
    "A third option was added once the scorer existed: a cheap, uncomfortable evening departure. Without it the corpus never exercised the behaviour the whole target selector exists for - a bargain climbing the list under Cheapest while its grade, which is scored at the reference profile, does not move. Three options that always sort the same way would have let a scorer that ignored the weights pass every test."
  ],
